LOCATION:LOWELL E. BAIER HALL/IU MAURER SCHOOL OF LAW
SUMMARY:ILJ Symposium: Evolving Frontiers in Criminal Law: Pregnancy\, Fa
 mily\, and Identity
DESCRIPTION:The Symposium originated from the book\, Pink Crime: Fighting
  Against the Criminalization of Motherhood\, Pregnancy\, and Queer Identi
 ty\, authored by Professor Valena Beety\, the Robert H. McKinney Professo
 r of Law at Indiana University Maurer School of Law and a founding board 
 member of the Indiana Innocence Project. Pink Crime focuses on the ways t
 hat criminal law is strategically used to limit the bodily autonomy of wo
 men and queer people\, combined with a discussion of how the system as a 
 whole targets the most vulnerable populations while allowing bias\, stigm
 a\, and unreliable evidence to influence prosecution decisions\, especial
 ly in situations where no crime occurred at all. This Symposium worked to
  expand upon Professor Beety's work in Pink Crime by bringing in expert p
 erspectives to illustrate how existing and developing legal mechanisms st
 rip away basic rights and lay the groundwork for more oppressive measures
  in the future. This area of law is evolving too quickly for large portio
 ns of the legal academy to keep up. Therefore\, this Symposium aims to an
 alyze the legal\, social\, and political dimensions of identity criminali
 zation and provide timely theory\, analysis\, and practical solutions for
  professionals to draw on as we move forward.ILJ associates are required 
 to attend at least two panels. Attendance will be taken.Panel one:  ILJ S
 ymposium: Opening Remarks &amp\; Prosecution of Pregnancyhttps://iu.zoom.
 us/webinar/register/WN_W_4FzIBRRsaxZQWLx-O5Bw (https://iu.zoom.us/webinar
 /register/WN_W_4FzIBRRsaxZQWLx-O5Bw)&#160\;Panel two:  ILJ Symposium: Cri
 minal Law After Dobbshttps://iu.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_50EaYXAiTDOEA
 5ouDYnhkw (https://iu.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_50EaYXAiTDOEA5ouDYnhkw)
 &#160\;Panel three:  ILJ Symposium: Family Regulation and Criminal Lawhtt
 ps://iu.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_KP47CXL4Rn6GzrdNEjOSpQ (https://iu.zo
 om.us/webinar/register/WN_KP47CXL4Rn6GzrdNEjOSpQ)&#160\;Panel four:  ILJ 
 Symposium: Criminalizing Queer Life and Familyhttps://iu.zoom.us/webinar/
 register/WN_tM-sch02TdKdlIlNL5URfA (https://iu.zoom.us/webinar/register/W
 N_tM-sch02TdKdlIlNL5URfA)&#160\;Panel five:  ILJ Symposium: Systemic Fail
 ures Along the Path to Wrongful Convictions &amp\; Closing Remarkshttps:/
 /iu.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_yocH6mKWQd-hWRjkezuLzA (https://iu.zoom.u
 s/webinar/register/WN_yocH6mKWQd-hWRjkezuLzA)&#160\;  Each of these five 
 lectures has been approved for 1 hour of CLE credit by the Indiana Office
  of Admissions and Continuing Education  We acknowledge IU Research and t
 he Research Conference Grant program for its generous funding and support
  of this symposium.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  The Symposium originated from the book\
 , <em>Pink Crime: Fighting Against the Criminalization of Motherhood\, Pr
 egnancy\, and Queer Identity</em>\, authored by Professor Valena Beety\, 
 the Robert H. McKinney Professor of Law at Indiana University Maurer Scho
 ol of Law and a founding board member of the Indiana Innocence Project. <
 em>Pink Crime</em> focuses on the ways that criminal law is strategically
  used to limit the bodily autonomy of women and queer people\, combined w
 ith a discussion of how the system as a whole targets the most vulnerable
  populations while allowing bias\, stigma\, and unreliable evidence to in
 fluence prosecution decisions\, especially in situations where no crime o
 ccurred at all. This Symposium worked to expand upon Professor Beety's wo
 rk in <em>Pink Crime</em> by bringing in expert perspectives to illustrat
 e how existing and developing legal mechanisms strip away basic rights an
 d lay the groundwork for more oppressive measures in the future. This are
 a of law is evolving too quickly for large portions of the legal academy 
 to keep up. Therefore\, this Symposium aims to analyze the legal\, social
 \, and political dimensions of identity criminalization and provide timel
 y theory\, analysis\, and practical solutions for professionals to draw o
 n as we move forward.</p><p><span style="text-decoration: underline\;">IL
 J associates are required to attend at least two panels. Attendance will 
 be taken.</span></p><p><strong>Panel one:</strong></p><p>  ILJ Symposium:
  Opening Remarks &amp\; Prosecution of Pregnancy</p><p><a href="https://i
 u.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_W_4FzIBRRsaxZQWLx-O5Bw">https://iu.zoom.us/
 webinar/register/WN_W_4FzIBRRsaxZQWLx-O5Bw</a>&#160\;</p><p><strong>Panel
  two:</strong></p><p>  ILJ Symposium: Criminal Law After Dobbs</p><p><a h
 ref="https://iu.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_50EaYXAiTDOEA5ouDYnhkw">https
 ://iu.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_50EaYXAiTDOEA5ouDYnhkw</a>&#160\;</p><p
 ><strong>Panel three:</strong></p><p>  ILJ Symposium: Family Regulation a
 nd Criminal Law</p><p><a href="https://iu.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_KP4
 7CXL4Rn6GzrdNEjOSpQ">https://iu.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_KP47CXL4Rn6Gz
 rdNEjOSpQ</a>&#160\;</p><p><strong>Panel four:</strong></p><p>  ILJ Sympo
 sium: Criminalizing Queer Life and Family</p><p><a href="https://iu.zoom.
 us/webinar/register/WN_tM-sch02TdKdlIlNL5URfA">https://iu.zoom.us/webinar
 /register/WN_tM-sch02TdKdlIlNL5URfA</a>&#160\;</p><p><strong>Panel five:<
 /strong></p><p>  ILJ Symposium: Systemic Failures Along the Path to Wrong
 ful Convictions &amp\; Closing Remarks</p><p><a href="https://iu.zoom.us/
 webinar/register/WN_yocH6mKWQd-hWRjkezuLzA">https://iu.zoom.us/webinar/re
 gister/WN_yocH6mKWQd-hWRjkezuLzA</a>&#160\;</p><p>  Each of these five le
 ctures has been approved for 1 hour of CLE credit by the Indiana Office o
 f Admissions and Continuing Education</p><p>  We acknowledge IU Research 
 and the Research Conference Grant program for its generous funding and su
 pport of this symposium.</p>
